   "id": "fortress",
   "title": "The hedgehog in the valley",
   "time": "Dec 1953 - Mar 1954",
   "narrative": "After the November 1953 parachute drop, de Castries' garrison turned the Muong Thanh valley into a ring of fortified hills named for women: Beatrice, Gabrielle and Anne-Marie on the north, Dominique and Eliane east of the Nam Rom, Huguette and Claudine west and south, and Isabelle six kilometres away at the reserve strip. The French relied on air supply and artillery to beat any assault. The Viet Minh, however, hauled guns by hand up the wooded hills and dug in around the valley.",
