  {
   "id": "beatrice",
   "title": "Beatrice falls",
   "time": "13 March 1954",
   "narrative": "On the evening of 13 March the Viet Minh guns opened up without warning. A shell struck the Beatrice command post and killed the Legion battalion commander and most of his staff, and Colonel Gaucher, who commanded the central sector, died a few minutes later. The 312th Division then sent in the 141st and 209th Regiments, and sappers cut the wire. By morning the Foreign Legion had lost the hill, and the French learned that their counter-battery fire could not find the enemy guns.",
