  {
   "id": "gabrielle",
   "title": "Gabrielle and the guns",
   "time": "14-15 March",
   "narrative": "The next night the 308th Division attacked Gabrielle, held by an Algerian battalion. Artillery fell for hours before the infantry advanced at 20:00, and a shell wounded the battalion commander at 04:00. A relief thrust by an exhausted Vietnamese paratroop battalion was pinned by shellfire. The Algerians withdrew at 08:00 on 15 March. The airstrip had already been closed by the bombardment, so every ration and shell now had to come down by parachute.",
