  {
   "id": "anne-marie",
   "title": "Anne-Marie dissolves",
   "time": "17 March",
   "narrative": "Anne-Marie in the north-west was held by Tai auxiliaries. Giap had spent weeks leaflet-dropping them with the argument that this was not their war, and the loss of Beatrice and Gabrielle broke their morale. Under morning fog on 17 March most of them walked away, leaving the French and a few remaining Tai to pull back. The garrison was now confined to the central ring and to distant Isabelle.",
