  {
   "id": "lull",
   "title": "Two weeks of quiet",
   "time": "17-30 March",
   "narrative": "The Viet Minh used the lull to tighten the ring and cut Isabelle off. Inside the camp the command cracked: de Castries withdrew to his bunker, and Colonel Langlais is often said to have taken effective control on 24 March, though that confrontation is disputed. Chief gunner Piroth, who had promised to out-shoot the enemy, died on 15 March. Supply flights were forced above 2,000 m, and a sortie on 28 March destroyed seventeen anti-aircraft machine guns near the strip.",
