  {
   "id": "eastern-assaults",
   "title": "Dominique and Eliane",
   "time": "30 March - 5 April",
   "narrative": "On 30 March the Viet Minh went for the two hill groups east of the river. The 312th took Dominique 1 and 2 at dusk, while the 316th captured Eliane 1 and half of Eliane 2. French 105 mm howitzers fired at zero elevation into the attackers, and counterattacks led by Langlais and Bigeard won back part of the ground. For several nights Eliane 2 and 4 changed hands under tanks and bayonets. The French held, but there were few reinforcements and the losses could not be replaced.",
