   "narrative": "Giap ordered an all-out attack on 7 May with more than 25,000 men. At 17:00 de Castries told Hanoi that the end was near and was ordered to fight on; soon afterward the radio went silent as the headquarters bunker was overrun. Roughly 18:20 saw only Lily, held by Moroccans, still resisting, and it surrendered that night. That night a break-out from the main camp failed, while at Isabelle about seventy of 1,700 men reached Laos. About 11,700 Frenchmen went into captivity.",
